          },
          "instructions": "Step through the explanation, then press Play to see what the forces do to the sliding box."
        },
        "steps": [
          {
            "text": "A box slides to the right after a push has ended. Before drawing any arrow, ask: what is pushing or pulling, and is it touching the box?",
            "cue": {
              "cue": "note",
              "args": {
                "text": "No agent, no force."
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "text": "Gravity acts without touching: the Earth pulls the box down with its weight.",
            "cue": {
              "cue": "add-vector",
              "args": {
                "vector": {
                  "id": "W",
                  "kind": "weight",
                  "label": "Weight (Earth)",
                  "agent": "Earth",
                  "magnitude": 19.6,
                  "angleDeg": -90
                }
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "text": "The floor touches the box: it pushes up (the normal force) and rubs against the sliding box (friction, backwards).",
            "cue": [
              {
                "cue": "add-vector",
                "args": {
                  "vector": {
                    "id": "N",
                    "kind": "normal",
                    "label": "Normal (floor)",
                    "agent": "floor",
                    "magnitude": 19.6,
                    "angleDeg": 90
                  }
                }
              },
              {
                "cue": "add-vector",
                "args": {
                  "vector": {
                    "id": "f",
                    "kind": "friction",
                    "label": "Friction (floor)",
                    "agent": "floor",
                    "magnitude": 5.9,
                    "angleDeg": 180
                  }
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Nothing else touches the box, so there is no 'force of motion'. It keeps moving by inertia while friction slows it. Press Play.",
            "cue": {
              "cue": "predict"
            }
          }
